# output AND 83 hand-written measurement probes under web/qa/tools/, which are neither generated nor
# regenerable - prompt 69 fixed two of them and could not commit the fixes.
#
# THE RULE STILL STANDS, and the remedy is the one this file already names: PROMOTION. A probe that
# a live run depends on belongs in tracked `web/scripts/`, which is where `geometry.mjs` went for
# exactly this reason (register: "in scripts/ rather than qa/tools/ because web/qa/ is gitignored").
#
# TWO HAVE BEEN PROMOTED, to web/scripts/probes/: s0-gaps.mjs and s3-spacing.mjs, the two prompt 69
# actually ran and fixed. Their originals were DELETED from web/qa/tools/ rather than left as second
# copies - an untracked duplicate of a measurement tool drifts invisibly, which is the defect being
# closed. Register 30 says why those two and not the other 82.
#
# The rest stays ignored and that is correct: it is qa-shots output plus closed-prompt archaeology.
# A filename search across prompts 55-60, handoff-status.md, the register and both contracts named
# none of it - though that search finds probes WRITTEN ABOUT, not probes RUN, so it is a floor on
# what deserves promotion and not a ceiling.
web/qa/
